#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""lg: a remote control for LG webOS TVs, in the terminal.

Usage:
  lg                     open the menu
  lg remote              control the TV with this computer's keyboard and mouse
  lg setup [IP]          find the TV on the network (or use IP) and pair with it
  lg on | off            turn the TV on (Wake-on-LAN) or off
  lg screen-on | screen-off
  lg volume [N|up|down]  show the volume, or change it
  lg mute | unmute
  lg play | pause | stop | rewind | forward
  lg input [ID]          list the inputs, or switch to one
  lg app [ID]            list the apps, or start one
  lg open URL            open a web page (YouTube links open in the YouTube app)
  lg notify TEXT         show a message on the TV
  lg button NAME         press a remote control button: HOME, BACK, UP, ENTER, ...
  lg type TEXT           type into the text field selected on the TV

lg needs only Python 3, plus whiptail or dialog for the menu. It talks to the
TV through the TV's own websocket API and keeps the pairing in
~/.config/lg/config.json.
"""

